On the seventh day of my internship, I focused on file and 
directory management in Linux. I continued reading the 
relevant sections of the Linux book and studied commands 
such as cp, mv, rm, and rmdir. I learned how files and 
directories can be copied, moved, renamed, and deleted
using the terminal.

I also studied different ways of viewing file contents. 
I reviewed the cat command and learned about commands 
such as less, head, and tail. I practiced using these 
commands in my Ubuntu environment while following the 
examples from the book.

After studying these topics, I continued solving 
beginner-level exercises on HackerRank. I tried 
to solve the problems by using the Linux commands 
that I had learned instead of directly looking at 
solutions. This helped me improve my understanding 
of how the commands can be used together.
